GLOBAL DECLARATIONS
  CAPABILITY hash.sha256
  ARTIFACT 0G-DECONSTRUCTION-STATE.md
  ARTIFACT 0H-CHECKPOINT-SUMMARY.md
END

SECTION invocation-identity-header
NUMBER 8.1
TITLE "Resume identity header"

GOAL
  Every invocation begins with the identity header, and the conforming runtime
  independently validates declared actions, exact read/write scope, loaded
  fingerprints, checkpoint freshness, and mode rights before commit.
END

FIELD INVOCATION-HEADER
  protocol-version                      -> string  required
  system-namespace                      -> string  required
  current-iteration                     -> string  required
  invocation-id                         -> id      required
  invocation-mode                       -> string  required
  human-hatch-action                    -> string  optional
  invocation-scope                      -> string  required
  persona                               -> string  optional
  persona-prefix                        -> string  optional
  persona-directory                     -> string  optional
  entry-cluster                         -> string  optional
  traversal-track                       -> string  optional
  active-pov                            -> string  optional
  active-pov-file                       -> string  optional
  active-question-ledger                -> string  optional
  environment-snapshot                  -> string  required
  max-traversal-depth                   -> int     required
  allowed-read-targets                  -> set<string> required
  allowed-write-targets                 -> set<string> required
  forbidden-write-targets               -> set<string> required
  loaded-checkpoint-fingerprint         -> hash    optional
END

RULE header-authorization
  GOAL
    The executor MUST declare its intended semantic actions against the identity
    header before writing. Active POV is POV-1 through POV-5. The conforming runtime
    MUST independently validate the declared actions, exact read/write scope, loaded
    fingerprints, checkpoint freshness, and mode rights before commit; an executor's
    self-assessment cannot authorize mutation.
  END
END

SECTION strict-single-scope
NUMBER 8.2
TITLE "Strict single-scope modes"

GOAL
  Discovery, Ticket Resolution, and Promotion Review bind exactly one persona,
  prefix, directory, cluster, track, POV, POV file, and at most one question ledger.
END

RULE strict-bindings
  GOAL
    Each strict mode has one semantic POV target and optional one semantic ledger
    target. Its fixed transactional sidecar bundle MAY append only directly produced
    rows or blocks in 10, 11, 12, 14, 16, persona-local shared buffers,
    personas/{persona-directory}/UNMAPPED-DISCOVERY-BUFFER.md, and 0G; these are
    assurance and audit side effects, not permission to change scope or another POV's
    semantics. Cross-POV outputs go to the bound ledger or persona-local buffers. An
    unmapped discovery MUST use the local buffer and requires Sequential Reconciliation
    before any later Discovery invocation.
  END
END

RULE wildcard-expansion
  GOAL
    A cluster containing wildcards MUST be expanded into concrete coordinates before a
    closing invocation. One invocation may traverse multiple atomic units reachable
    from its one concrete root, subject to depth and frontier rules, but may not switch
    roots, personas, POVs, or tracks.
  END
END

RULE alfa-start-behavior
  GOAL
    ALFA is the first bounded discovery iteration. Every POV may log questions
    immediately; no maturity phase may suppress cross-boundary ambiguity. On large
    repositories, ALFA MUST still obey concrete cluster, track, persona, POV, and depth
    isolation. Branches beyond the bound become frontier records and tickets rather
    than an attempted full-tree sweep.
  END
END

SECTION concurrent-persona-traversal
NUMBER 8.6
TITLE "Concurrent persona traversal"

GOAL
  Personas MAY run concurrently in one named iteration but MUST NOT write canonical
  shared POV or shared question files directly.
END

RULE concurrency-buffers
  GOAL
    Shared component discoveries go to
    personas/{persona-directory}/SHARED-STAGING-BUFFER.md; outbound shared questions go
    to personas/{persona-directory}/SHARED-QUESTIONS-BUFFER.md; unmapped coordinates go
    to personas/{persona-directory}/UNMAPPED-DISCOVERY-BUFFER.md with a same-transaction
    FRT; persona-owned invocation pointers may be written immediately; depromotion is
    annotated R-DEPROMOTION-PENDING and deferred.
  END
END

RULE sequential-reconciliation-merge
  GOAL
    Sequential Reconciliation collects, deterministically sorts, and deduplicates all
    buffer classes, promotion requests, and synthesis gaps; merges compatible claims
    without improperly raising BLOCK-CONFIDENCE-RANK or losing profile detail; records
    contradictions; merges persona sets; commits shared records and tickets; merges
    unmapped discoveries into 0A; creates required ticket and frontier work from GAP
    records; executes promotion and depromotion atomically; updates assurance links;
    and purges consumed buffers atomically. No later Discovery invocation may begin
    while an unmapped-discovery buffer contains a Pending-Merge entry.
  END
END

SECTION stale-checkpoint-guard
NUMBER 8.7
TITLE "Stale checkpoint guard"

GOAL
  Before writing, compare loaded checkpoint and source fingerprints with target record
  versions.
END

RULE stale-guard
  GOAL
    If any target changed after the checkpoint, stop and request a refreshed read set.
    Changed serialized fingerprints invalidate affected normalized maps, source
    records, claims, coverage, and downstream blocks before further mutation.
  END
END

SECTION invocation-log
NUMBER 8.8
TITLE "0G invocation log"

GOAL
  Append the invocation log record after every invocation; 0H MAY compress current
  active states but MUST include its source 0G range and fingerprint.
END

FIELD INVOCATION-LOG
  identity-header-summary                          -> string required
  cold-resume-result-check-fingerprint             -> string required
  declared-semantic-actions-runtime-authorization-result -> string required
  loaded-files-fingerprints                        -> string required
  mutation-summary                                 -> string required
  tickets-created-updated                          -> string required
  frontiers-created-closed                         -> string required
  unmapped-discoveries-gap-records-buffered-merged-or-disposed -> string required
  exports-acquired-requested                       -> string required
  src-cmp-clm-ids-updated                          -> string required
  evidence-changes                                 -> string required
  promotion-depromotion                            -> string required
  coverage-reconciliation-changes                  -> string required
  stale-propagation                                -> string required
  next-required-loads                              -> string required
END

RULE invocation-log-append
  GOAL
    The appended record heading is [ITERATION] - [INVOCATION-ID] - [Scope] - [Mode].
    When 0H is used to authorize a later Discovery invocation, it MUST also include a
    fingerprinted global count and list of every persona-local Pending-Merge unmapped
    discovery; otherwise the full-buffer fallback read in §8.4 is required.
  END
END
